<title>JAPAN: Kubo says extra budget should be adopted early '97.</title>
<headline>Kubo says extra budget should be adopted early '97.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Minister of Finance Wataru Kubo told a news conference on Wednesday that a supplementary budget should be introduced in the early stages of a regular parliamentary session to be convened in January.</p>
<p>However, he added that at the moment the economic and fiscal situation did not warrant a supplementary budget including extra public works spending to stimulate the economy.</p>
</text>
